Loom patch (loomster#58): opt-in Cognito endpoint override for a local emulator.

Applied to vendor/loom by scripts/vendor-loom.sh, which checks it first and
fails if it no longer applies, so a Loom bump surfaces it. Nothing here goes
upstream.

Loom v1.9.0 hardcodes https://cognito-idp.<region>.amazonaws.com as the Cognito
issuer and JWKS base (backend) and as the InitiateAuth endpoint (frontend), so
tokens from Floci's Cognito can't validate and the login form can't reach it.

- backend: LOOM_COGNITO_ENDPOINT_URL, when set, replaces that base for the
  issuer and JWKS URL. The JWKS fetch for this operator-set URL skips the SSRF
  guard (net_guard.safe_get), which refuses Floci's private plain-http address.
  Access tokens are otherwise validated exactly as Loom validates real Cognito
  ones.
- frontend: build arg VITE_COGNITO_ENDPOINT_URL, when set, is where the login
  form posts InitiateAuth, RespondToAuthChallenge and the token refresh.

Both unset (every real deployment), the code paths are upstream's.

